1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Akash asks what satellite evidence supports, and which road-access conclusions depend on unknowns.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
It joins before-and-after radar, optical observations, elevation and pre-event OpenStreetMap.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Its strongest feature is a conditional access proof: test uncertain roads and keep the evidence.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
This actual saved radar map comes from the completed Rasuwa case for 26 August 2026.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
There are 25,237 newly predicted water candidate cells. They are not confirmed damage.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Radar jointly assesses 1,666,783 of 2,480,036 cells; 813,253 remain unknown.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Before-and-after processing uses matched radar sources from 16 and 28 August. Local accuracy remains unproved.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The optical layer retains its native grid and its own observation denominator.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Only 68,801 of 620,008 cells are jointly assessed: 11.10 percent.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
A further 551,207 cells remain unknown. Cloud and missing support are not filled with certainty.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The 1,060 surface-change candidates use fixed hypotheses. They are not validated debris classifications.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The current browser can inspect saved access evidence. This does not execute a new satellite run.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Within this AOI: 14 settlements are undetermined, six unmapped, and two baseline disconnected.

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The graph fixes baseline targets and checks uncertain road groups under all-open and all-closed scenarios.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Witness paths and cut certificates can be checked independently. They do not establish safe passage or observed closures.

16
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
The recorded known-case workflow completed all 14 stages in 171.07 seconds on the local computer.

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Radar, elevation and pre-event OSM were verified cached inputs. This is not a cold-acquisition timing.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
New Sentinel-2 acquisition received 60,069,247 bytes. Source identities and output receipts remain inspectable.

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Historical-map provider failures are retained. Arbitrary judge-selected raw-data reliability remains unproved.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:19,000
The unchanged Sen1Floods11 water benchmark reports 43.89 percent IoU and 79.99 percent precision.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Water recall is 49.30 percent. This benchmark does not validate Himalayan flood, debris or infrastructure damage.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Earlier EMSR927 comparisons are checking-only, involve different classes and fail internal coverage gates. No accuracy is invented.

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Open the public saved-evidence website to inspect maps, source facts and conditional access results.

24
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Use the separate local console and documented prerequisites to plan and run bounded satellite processing.

25
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
The static website does not run that backend or the optional local Qwen copilot.

26
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Original code is MIT. Data retains upstream terms. AI assistance is disclosed. This is an educational evidence prototype.
